@symbol runGet

doc {
  Applicable context is deterministic retrieval, not a new explanation or an authority decision.

  Default get keeps exact path/symbol selection. context=true returns symbol → file → enclosing folders → root as separate layers, including ancestors when the target has no direct tether. File context excludes child symbols; references are checked dependencies, not inheritance edges.

  Bodies and examples remain opaque source content. Git commits identify mechanical baselines, not operator approval. No field certifies truth, intent, compliance, or execution of an example. Empty facts must be read with coverage and unchecked comparisons.

  Missing targets and ambiguous or unexamined symbol selectors fail explicitly. A surviving sidecar can still retrieve doctrine for its missing host. Path containment is checked before normalization. Evidence is source-path scoped, not occurrence-specific.

  Get performs live analysis of the requested checkout and never reads a search cache. Search freshness, immutable snapshots, and occurrence-qualified selectors are separate work, not guarantees of this command.
}
